win32u, winewayland, explorer: a tray icon's Win32 menu opens at the icon, drawn by the desktop's tray (dbusmenu).

With patch 123 a tray icon's right click reached the application, whose TrackPopupMenu window KWin put in the middle of
the screen with a taskbar entry. Windows opens it at the icon. His call (C178): tray menus at the icon, drawn by the
desktop. Every SNI tray draws a menu at the icon when the item exports one over com.canonical.dbusmenu, so the item's
Menu is now a dbusmenu, filled from the application's own HMENU:
- when the tray opens the menu (AboutToShow on the root, with the "opened" event Plasma and GNOME send), explorer marks
  the icon's window (WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_PROP) and relays the right click as before;
- TrackPopupMenu on a marked window sends WM_ENTERMENULOOP / WM_INITMENU / WM_INITMENUPOPUP as on Windows (and
  WM_INITMENUPOPUP to each submenu, before the menu shows rather than when it opens), copies the items to Shell_TrayWnd
  (WM_COPYDATA, explorer hands it to the driver), and runs a message loop until the tray's menu closes;
- the tray's "clicked" gives the result a click in the Win32 menu gives (WM_COMMAND, WM_MENUCOMMAND for
  MNS_NOTIFYBYPOS, or the id with TPM_RETURNCMD), "closed" gives none (Qt's "closed" comes before "clicked": 400 ms);
- labels keep mnemonics (& -> _, && -> &, _ -> __) and drop the "\tCtrl+O" part; separators, grayed items, checked
  and radio items, submenus. Item ids carry the menu's revision, so no host keeps an old item's properties.
Hosts differ, measured in the lab:
- GNOME's AppIndicator extension calls AboutToShow ahead of time (at attach) and never calls ContextMenu: under 123 a
  right click did nothing there. An AboutToShow without an "opened" event gets "nothing new" and the application gets
  no click (Windows sends tray messages only on clicks); the root then holds one disabled item (the tooltip) until the
  first menu comes, since GNOME opens only a non-empty menu. Hosts that send no "opened" at all (waybar) get the menu
  when they ask later than 3 s after the item appeared.
- An application whose menu is not a Win32 menu (Qt's QMenu: Filmora) sends nothing; after a second the tray is told
  nothing is new and the application's window shows as before; Plasma then shows no menu of its own.
Not covered: non-Win32 menus still open where the compositor puts them (KWin, sway and Hyprland offer
zwlr_layer_shell_v1, GNOME does not; not used); owner-drawn and system menus keep the Win32 popup; item bitmaps;
WM_MENUSELECT while hovering; a host that never sends "closed" (waybar) leaves the application in TrackPopupMenu
(still processing its messages) until the next click or menu; waybar draws the very first menu in a popup sized for the
placeholder (scroll arrow), later ones at full size; swaybar's own tray calls ContextMenu (no dbusmenu), so there the
Win32 menu window shows as with 123 (sway tiles it).

Lab, 179 + 123 + this (lab 11.10-179d), tray test program (agents/dbusmenu/menutest: check set in WM_INITMENUPOPUP,
radio, grayed, submenu filled in its WM_INITMENUPOPUP, default item, "&Open\tCtrl+O", "Save_as && quit", separator):
- scripted dbusmenu host: the menu came 1-12 ms after AboutToShow, every property as above; TPM_RETURNCMD 13 / 21
  (submenu) / 0 (closed) / 0 (grayed clicked, then closed); "closed" then "clicked" 21; AboutToShowGroup 10; WM_COMMAND
  12 / 20 / cancel TRUE without a command / 99 (exit); WM_MENUCOMMAND position + menu (13, 21, 99); a second open
  without "closed" ends the first with 0 and shows the second; legacy (WM_RBUTTONUP) and NOTIFYICON_VERSION_4 apps;
- nested Plasma 6: the menu at the icon in Plasma's style, submenu, Sub B -> 21, Escape 0 (2/2), Large 13 (2/2),
  click outside 0 (2/2), unchecked item without a box; Filmora's Qt menu (2/2 + 1/1): its own window, no Plasma menu;
- GNOME with the AppIndicator extension (podman): no click at attach; the menu at the icon in GNOME's style, Large 13
  (2/2), Escape 0, click outside 0; first open on a fresh icon 3/3 (1 fail right after the session started, not seen
  again);
- waybar (sway, podman): from the second open the menu at the icon, Large 13, checked/unchecked right.
- kill switch NEUTRON_SNI_DBUSMENU=0: Menu /NO_DBUSMENU; Plasma: the Win32 menu in the middle with a taskbar entry (123).
Lab trap: the Unix side of win32u/winewayland has 32-bit wchar_t, so L"__wine_..." property names read as "_" and
the request and its result overwrote each other (a second open without "closed" hung); WCHAR initializers fix it.

Kill switch NEUTRON_SNI_DBUSMENU=0.

--- a/dlls/win32u/menu.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/menu.c
@@ -4646,6 +4646,198 @@
     exit_tracking( hwnd, FALSE );
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON sni-dbusmenu (2026-11-04, his C178: tray menus at the icon, drawn by the desktop).
+ *
+ * On Windows a tray icon's context menu opens at the icon, in the taskbar. With the icon in the desktop's own tray
+ * (winewayland's StatusNotifierItem, patch 123) the application's menu window cannot be placed there: a Wayland
+ * client does not position its windows, so KWin put it in the middle of the screen with a taskbar entry. The tray
+ * draws a menu at the icon itself when the item exports one over com.canonical.dbusmenu, so while the shell waits
+ * for an icon's menu (WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_PROP on the icon's window, see ntuser.h), TrackPopupMenu on that window does
+ * what it does on Windows up to the point of showing the popup (WM_ENTERMENULOOP, WM_INITMENU, WM_INITMENUPOPUP),
+ * hands the items to the shell, and runs a message loop until the desktop's menu closes; the chosen item then gives
+ * the same WM_COMMAND / WM_MENUCOMMAND or TPM_RETURNCMD result as a click in the Win32 menu would.
+ * Differences: submenus get their WM_INITMENUPOPUP before the menu shows instead of when they open; owner-drawn
+ * menus, system menus and a shell that does not take the menu keep the Win32 popup; item bitmaps are not shown.
+ * Kill switch NEUTRON_SNI_DBUSMENU=0. */
+static BOOL neutron_tray_dbusmenu(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_SNI_DBUSMENU" ); on = !(e && e[0] == '0'); }
+    return on;
+}
+
+static const WCHAR tray_menu_propW[] = WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_PROP_INIT;
+static const WCHAR tray_menu_resultW[] = WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_RESULT_PROP_INIT;
+
+struct tray_menu_capture
+{
+    struct systray_menu_item *items;
+    struct { HMENU menu; UINT pos; UINT_PTR id; } *entries;
+    WCHAR *text;
+    UINT   count, max;
+    UINT   text_len, text_max;
+    BOOL   unsupported;
+};
+
+static UINT tray_menu_add_text( struct tray_menu_capture *c, const WCHAR *str )
+{
+    UINT len = wcslen( str ) + 1, offset = c->text_len;
+
+    if (c->text_len + len > c->text_max)
+    {
+        UINT max = max( c->text_max * 2, c->text_len + len + 256 );
+        WCHAR *text = realloc( c->text, max * sizeof(WCHAR) );
+        if (!text) { c->unsupported = TRUE; return ~0u; }
+        c->text = text;
+        c->text_max = max;
+    }
+    memcpy( c->text + c->text_len, str, len * sizeof(WCHAR) );
+    c->text_len += len;
+    return offset;
+}
+
+static void tray_menu_capture( struct tray_menu_capture *c, HWND hwnd, HMENU handle, INT parent, UINT flags,
+                               int depth )
+{
+    struct menu *menu;
+    UINT i;
+
+    if (depth > 8) { c->unsupported = TRUE; return; }
+    for (i = 0; !c->unsupported; i++)
+    {
+        struct systray_menu_item *item;
+        HMENU submenu = 0;
+        UINT index;
+
+        /* WM_INITMENUPOPUP for an earlier submenu may have changed this menu: look it up for every item */
+        if (!(menu = unsafe_menu_ptr( handle )) || i >= menu->nItems) break;
+        if (c->count == c->max)
+        {
+            UINT max = c->max ? c->max * 2 : 32;
+            void *items = realloc( c->items, max * sizeof(*c->items) );
+            void *entries = items ? realloc( c->entries, max * sizeof(*c->entries) ) : NULL;
+            if (items) c->items = items;
+            if (!items || !entries) { c->unsupported = TRUE; break; }
+            c->entries = entries;
+            c->max = max;
+        }
+        index = c->count++;
+        item = &c->items[index];
+        item->parent = parent;
+        item->type = menu->items[i].fType & (MFT_SEPARATOR | MFT_RADIOCHECK | MFT_BITMAP | MFT_OWNERDRAW | MF_POPUP);
+        item->state = menu->items[i].fState;
+        item->text = ~0u;
+        c->entries[index].menu = handle;
+        c->entries[index].pos = i;
+        c->entries[index].id = menu->items[i].wID;
+        if (item->type & MFT_OWNERDRAW) c->unsupported = TRUE;
+        if (IS_STRING_ITEM( menu->items[i].fType ) && menu->items[i].text)
+            item->text = tray_menu_add_text( c, menu->items[i].text );
+        if ((item->type & MF_POPUP) && menu->items[i].hSubMenu) submenu = menu->items[i].hSubMenu;
+        if (submenu)
+        {
+            if (!(flags & TPM_NONOTIFY)) send_message( hwnd, WM_INITMENUPOPUP, (WPARAM)submenu, i );
+            tray_menu_capture( c, hwnd, submenu, index, flags, depth + 1 );
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/* the shell shows the menu; TRUE with *ret set when it did, FALSE to show the Win32 popup */
+static BOOL tray_menu_show( HMENU handle, UINT flags, HWND hwnd, UINT request, BOOL *ret )
+{
+    static const WCHAR trayW[] = {'S','h','e','l','l','_','T','r','a','y','W','n','d',0};
+    UNICODE_STRING tray_class = RTL_CONSTANT_STRING( trayW );
+    struct tray_menu_capture c = { 0 };
+    struct systray_menu_data *data;
+    COPYDATASTRUCT cds;
+    UINT result = 0, size;
+    BOOL quit = FALSE;
+    HWND tray;
+    MSG msg;
+
+    tray_menu_capture( &c, hwnd, handle, -1, flags, 0 );
+    if (c.unsupported || !c.count || !(tray = NtUserFindWindowEx( 0, 0, &tray_class, NULL, 0 ))) goto failed;
+
+    size = offsetof( struct systray_menu_data, items[c.count] ) + c.text_len * sizeof(WCHAR);
+    if (!(data = malloc( size ))) goto failed;
+    data->size = size;
+    data->request = request;
+    data->count = c.count;
+    memcpy( data->items, c.items, c.count * sizeof(*c.items) );
+    memcpy( &data->items[c.count], c.text, c.text_len * sizeof(WCHAR) );
+    cds.dwData = WINE_SYSTRAY_MENU_DATA;
+    cds.cbData = size;
+    cds.lpData = data;
+    result = send_message_timeout( tray, WM_COPYDATA, (WPARAM)hwnd, (LPARAM)&cds, SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG, 2000, FALSE );
+    free( data );
+    if (result != TRUE) goto failed;
+    TRACE( "menu %p (%u items) shown by the tray for %p\n", handle, c.count, hwnd );
+
+    /* as in a menu loop, the application keeps running until the menu closes */
+    result = 0;
+    for (;;)
+    {
+        UINT_PTR value = (UINT_PTR)NtUserGetProp( hwnd, tray_menu_resultW );
+
+        if (value && HIWORD( value ) == LOWORD( request ))
+        {
+            NtUserRemoveProp( hwnd, tray_menu_resultW );
+            result = LOWORD( value );
+            break;
+        }
+        if (!is_window( hwnd ) || !is_window( tray )) break;
+        NtUserMsgWaitForMultipleObjectsEx( 0, NULL, 100, QS_ALLINPUT, 0 );
+        while (NtUserPeekMessage( &msg, 0, 0, 0, PM_REMOVE ))
+        {
+            if (msg.message == WM_QUIT)
+            {
+                NtUserPostQuitMessage( msg.wParam );
+                quit = TRUE;
+                break;
+            }
+            NtUserTranslateMessage( &msg, 0 );
+            NtUserDispatchMessage( &msg );
+        }
+        if (quit) break;
+    }
+
+    *ret = (flags & TPM_RETURNCMD) ? 0 : TRUE;
+    if (result && result <= c.count && is_window( hwnd ))
+    {
+        const struct systray_menu_item *item = &c.items[result - 1];
+        struct menu *menu = unsafe_menu_ptr( c.entries[result - 1].menu );
+        struct menu *top = unsafe_menu_ptr( handle );
+
+        TRACE( "tray chose item %u (id %#lx)\n", result, (long)c.entries[result - 1].id );
+        if (!(item->type & (MF_POPUP | MFT_SEPARATOR)) && !(item->state & (MF_GRAYED | MF_DISABLED)))
+        {
+            /* exec_focused_item */
+            if (!(flags & TPM_RETURNCMD))
+            {
+                DWORD style = (menu ? menu->dwStyle : 0) | (top ? top->dwStyle : 0);
+                if (style & MNS_NOTIFYBYPOS)
+                    NtUserPostMessage( hwnd, WM_MENUCOMMAND, c.entries[result - 1].pos,
+                                       (LPARAM)c.entries[result - 1].menu );
+                else
+                    NtUserPostMessage( hwnd, WM_COMMAND, c.entries[result - 1].id, 0 );
+            }
+            else *ret = c.entries[result - 1].id;
+        }
+    }
+    if (is_window( hwnd )) send_message( hwnd, WM_MENUSELECT, MAKEWPARAM( 0, 0xffff ), 0 );
+    free( c.items );
+    free( c.entries );
+    free( c.text );
+    return TRUE;
+
+failed:
+    TRACE( "menu %p stays a Win32 popup (unsupported %d, %u items)\n", handle, c.unsupported, c.count );
+    free( c.items );
+    free( c.entries );
+    free( c.text );
+    return FALSE;
+}
+
 /**********************************************************************
  *           NtUserTrackPopupMenuEx   (win32u.@)
  */
@@ -4654,6 +4846,7 @@
 {
     struct menu *menu;
     BOOL ret = FALSE;
+    UINT tray_request = 0;
 
     TRACE( "hmenu %p flags %04x (%d,%d) hwnd %p params %p rect %s\n",
            handle, flags, x, y, hwnd, params,
@@ -4671,6 +4864,11 @@
         return FALSE;
     }
 
+    /* NEUTRON sni-dbusmenu: is the tray waiting for this window's menu? */
+    if (neutron_tray_dbusmenu() && !(menu->wFlags & MF_SYSMENU) &&
+        (tray_request = HandleToUlong( NtUserGetProp( hwnd, tray_menu_propW ))))
+        NtUserRemoveProp( hwnd, tray_menu_propW );
+
     if (init_popup( hwnd, handle, flags ))
     {
         init_tracking( hwnd, handle, TRUE, flags );
@@ -4683,7 +4881,9 @@
             init_sys_menu_popup( handle, get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ),
                                  get_class_long( hwnd, GCL_STYLE, FALSE ));
 
-        if (show_popup( hwnd, handle, 0, flags, x, y, 0, 0 ))
+        if (tray_request && tray_menu_show( handle, flags, hwnd, tray_request, &ret ))
+            ;  /* the desktop's tray showed it */
+        else if (show_popup( hwnd, handle, 0, flags, x, y, 0, 0 ))
             ret = track_menu( handle, flags | TPM_POPUPMENU, 0, 0, hwnd,
                               params ? &params->rcExclude : NULL );
         exit_tracking( hwnd, TRUE );
